Find the gradient of the interval joining $A(-4, -3)$ and $B(0, 5)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.55]
\draw[step=1,gray!25,very thin] (-5,-5) grid (5,5);
\draw[<->] (-5.5,0)--(5.5,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-5.5)--(0,5.5) node[above]{$y$};
\foreach \i in {-5,-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5} \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\i,0){$\i$};
\foreach \i in {-5,-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5} \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,\i){$\i$};
\draw[thick,blue] (-4,-3)--(0,5);
\fill (-4,-3) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt,font=\scriptsize] at (-4,-3){$A(-4,-3)$};
\fill (0,5) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt,font=\scriptsize] at (0,5){$B(0,5)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

